1
00:00:00,735 --> 00:00:02,335
(birds singing,
insects trilling)

2
00:00:02,337 --> 00:00:04,837
SHELDON:
It's nice to get back to nature.

3
00:00:05,079 --> 00:00:06,809
(Sheldon:)Why don't I do this more often?

4
00:00:10,685 --> 00:00:13,485
(Sheldon:)What a beautiful forest.

5
00:00:13,488 --> 00:00:15,258
(gasps delightedly)

6
00:00:15,256 --> 00:00:18,226
(Sheldon:)Hello, little butterfly.

7
00:00:19,381 --> 00:00:20,781
(Sheldon:)What's your Na...

8
00:00:20,782 --> 00:00:22,852
(screams)

9
00:00:22,851 --> 00:00:24,451
(Leonard:)Whatcha doing?

10
00:00:24,452 --> 00:00:27,182
(Sheldon:)I was enjoying
some virtual reality,

11
00:00:27,188 --> 00:00:30,188
(Sheldon:)until you ruined it
with your actual face.

12
00:00:30,191 --> 00:00:32,491
(Penny:)What am I smelling?

13
00:00:32,494 --> 00:00:33,794
(Sheldon:)Oh, it's car
air freshener.

14
00:00:33,795 --> 00:00:36,765
(Sheldon:)I was simulating
the smell of the forest.

15
00:00:36,765 --> 00:00:38,735
(Penny:)That's not what
the forest smells like.

16
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:40,903
(Sheldon:)Well, how would I know?

17
00:00:43,305 --> 00:00:44,405
(Leonard:)Why are you pretending
to be outdoors?

18
00:00:44,406 --> 00:00:45,406
(Leonard:)You hate it.

19
00:00:45,407 --> 00:00:46,577
(Sheldon:)Hmm? Oh.

20
00:00:46,574 --> 00:00:48,374
(Sheldon:)Amy showed me a compelling study

21
00:00:48,376 --> 00:00:50,276
(Sheldon:)that demonstrated
the cognitive benefit

22
00:00:50,278 --> 00:00:51,848
(Sheldon:)of spending time
in the wilderness.

23
00:00:51,846 --> 00:00:53,246
(Leonard:)Buddy, I am ready
to drive you

24
00:00:53,248 --> 00:00:54,878
(Leonard:)into the wilderness
any time you want

25
00:00:54,883 --> 00:00:56,653
(Leonard:)and leave you there.

26
00:00:56,651 --> 00:00:59,751
(Sheldon:)Well, make your jokes,
but some of the participants

27
00:00:59,754 --> 00:01:02,654
(Sheldon:)who spent four days in the woods
away from all technology

28
00:01:02,657 --> 00:01:06,097
reported a 50% gain in reasoning
skills upon their return.

29
00:01:06,094 --> 00:01:09,964
(Penny:)Okay, if that's true, why aren't
there more genius squirrels?

30
00:01:12,934 --> 00:01:15,364
(Sheldon:)You may need this
more than I do.

31
00:01:16,571 --> 00:01:20,211
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

